.TH XD\-SECURITY 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-security \- the Windows Security dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-security
.YS
.SY xd\-security
.B \-\-change\-password
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-security
is Windows 2000's Windows Security dialog, which Ctrl+Alt+Delete opens in
the Classic style: who is logged on and since when, and Lock Computer,
Log Off, Shut Down, Change Password and Task Manager.
.PP
Change Password runs
.BR passwd (1)
for the user, answering its prompts, so the system's password rules
apply.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-change\-password
Only the Change Password dialog.
It must be the first argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-lock (1),
.BR xd\-shutdown (1),
.BR xd\-taskmgr (1),
.BR passwd (1)
